-- title:
--   Distinct minimal primes over p together with 1/j generate the unit ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$. Let $A =$ `chartAlgInf (N*p) p` be the subalgebra of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull (N*p)`, over the coefficient ring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), consisting of those elements of the field that are integral over the subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, where $j =$ `jFull (N*p)` is the element of the field given by the $q$-expansion `jq`; thus $A$ is the integral closure of [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8)$[\,j^{-1}\,]$ in the modular function field of full level $Np$. Let `jInvChartInf (N*p) p` denote the element $j^{-1}$ of $A$. Let $P$ and $P'$ be ideals of $A$, each a minimal prime over the principal ideal generated by the image of the integer $p$ in $A$, and assume $P \neq P'$. The assertion is that $$P + P' + j^{-1}A = A,$$ i.e. the supremum of $P$, $P'$ and the ideal generated by `jInvChartInf (N*p) p` is the whole of $A$.
--
--   In classical terms: in the pole chart of the integral model of the curve of full level $Np$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, no prime containing both $p$ and $1/j$ — no cusp of the fibre at $p$ — lies on two distinct irreducible components of that fibre, the cusps being unibranch points of the special fibre. It feeds the analysis of the fibre at $p$ of the Igusa-type model, being used in [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.fst_pullback_comp_mem_range_iotaFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.fst_pullback_comp_mem_range_iotaFin) and in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.jInvChartInf_not_mem_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.jInvChartInf_not_mem_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul).
